---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Prism from "prismjs";
import "prismjs/components/prism-lua.js";
import "prismjs/components/prism-toml.js";
import { Check, Copy } from "lucide-static";

const highlightPortalCommand = (code) => Prism.highlight(code, {
  "portal-subcommand": {
    pattern: /(?<=\belio\s+portal\s+)(?:enable|status|disable)\b/,
  },
}, "portal-command");
const highlightLua = (code) => Prism.highlight(code, Prism.languages.lua, "lua");
const highlightToml = (code) => Prism.highlight(code, Prism.languages.toml, "toml");
const portalSnippet = `[portal]
terminal = "kitty"`;
const hyprlandSnippet = `-- Matches the app ID/class.
hl.window_rule({
  name = "elio-file-chooser-class",
  match = { class = "^io\\\\.github\\\\.elio_fm\\\\.elio\\\\.filechooser$" },
  float = true,
  center = true,
})

-- Matches the window title.
hl.window_rule({
  name = "elio-file-chooser-title",
  match = { title = "^elio File Chooser$" },
  float = true,
  center = true,
})`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="elio docs: file chooser"
  description="Use elio as your XDG FileChooser portal for desktop applications on Linux and FreeBSD."
  currentPath="/docs/file-chooser/"
  heading="File chooser"
  lead="Using elio as your XDG FileChooser portal for desktop applications."
>
  <section class="docs-section docs-section-first">
    <div class="docs-section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">XDG DESKTOP PORTAL</p>
      <h2 class="docs-section-title">Set up elio as your file chooser</h2>
      <p>Available on Linux and FreeBSD.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-two-up docs-align-start">
      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card docs-tight-command-card docs-recommended-card">
        <div class="command-block" data-command-block>
          <button class="command-copy" type="button" data-copy-command data-copy-state="idle" aria-label="Copy command" title="Copy command">
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="copy" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Copy}></span>
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="check" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Check}></span>
          </button>
          <pre class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash" set:html={highlightPortalCommand("elio portal enable")}></code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-command-note">Detects your terminal, enables FileChooser routing, and restarts <code class="docs-inline-code">xdg-desktop-portal</code> to apply the change.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card">
        <h3>Supported requests</h3>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><span>Choosing one or more files.</span></li>
          <li><span>Choosing one or more folders.</span></li>
          <li><span>Saving a file through Save As mode.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <article class="doc-card docs-callout-card">
      <h3>Per-desktop setup</h3>
      <p>Run <code>elio portal enable</code> in each desktop session where you want elio to handle file chooser requests.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="doc-card docs-callout-card">
      <h3>Update Shell integration</h3>
      <p>If you installed Shell integration before 1.13.0 update it by running <code>elio shell install</code> again and restarting your shell so it passes <code>elio portal</code> commands through.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <div class="docs-section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">MANAGEMENT</p>
      <h2 class="docs-section-title">Check or disable the portal</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-two-up docs-align-start docs-portal-management-cards">
      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card docs-tight-command-card">
        <h3>Check status</h3>
        <div class="command-block" data-command-block>
          <button class="command-copy" type="button" data-copy-command data-copy-state="idle" aria-label="Copy status command" title="Copy status command">
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="copy" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Copy}></span>
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="check" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Check}></span>
          </button>
          <pre class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash" set:html={highlightPortalCommand("elio portal status")}></code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-command-note">Shows portal metadata and the active FileChooser routing.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card docs-tight-command-card">
        <h3>Disable the portal</h3>
        <div class="command-block" data-command-block>
          <button class="command-copy" type="button" data-copy-command data-copy-state="idle" aria-label="Copy disable command" title="Copy disable command">
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="copy" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Copy}></span>
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="check" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Check}></span>
          </button>
          <pre class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash" set:html={highlightPortalCommand("elio portal disable")}></code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-command-note">Restores FileChooser routing for every desktop configuration managed by elio.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <div class="docs-section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">TERMINAL</p>
      <h2 class="docs-section-title">Setting the terminal manually</h2>
      <p>To change the terminal used, set it in <code>config.toml</code>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-two-up docs-align-start">
      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card docs-config-example-card">
        <div class="command-block docs-config-code" data-command-block>
          <button class="command-copy" type="button" data-copy-command data-copy-state="idle" aria-label="Copy portal terminal config" title="Copy portal terminal config">
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="copy" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Copy}></span>
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="check" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Check}></span>
          </button>
          <pre class="language-toml"><code class="language-toml" set:html={highlightToml(portalSnippet)}></code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-command-note">Run <code class="docs-inline-code">elio portal enable</code> afterward to restart <code class="docs-inline-code">xdg-desktop-portal</code> and apply the change.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card">
        <p><code class="docs-inline-code">elio portal enable</code> only saves a detected terminal when you have not set one, so it will not override a terminal you set.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/configuration/#portal">View configuration →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <div class="docs-section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">WINDOW RULES</p>
      <h2 class="docs-section-title">Tiling window manager configuration</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-detail-stack">
      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card">
        <p>Many tiling window managers support per-window rules. Depending on the window manager, rules can match the chooser’s app ID/class <code class="docs-inline-code">io.github.elio_fm.elio.filechooser</code> or title <code class="docs-inline-code">elio File Chooser</code>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="doc-card docs-card-tight docs-detail-card">
        <h3>Hyprland example</h3>
        <p>This example matches both identifiers and makes the chooser floating and centered.</p>
        <div class="command-block docs-config-code" data-command-block>
          <button class="command-copy" type="button" data-copy-command data-copy-state="idle" aria-label="Copy Hyprland window rule" title="Copy Hyprland window rule">
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="copy" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Copy}></span>
            <span class="command-copy-icon" data-copy-icon="check" aria-hidden="true" set:html={Check}></span>
          </button>
          <pre class="language-lua"><code class="language-lua" set:html={highlightLua(hyprlandSnippet)}></code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
